          "path": "_m/d/n/h/t/tallulah-gorge-wp/tallulah-falls-thomas.jpg",
          "filename": "Tallulah Falls 7151.jpg",
          "caption": "Tallulah Falls. Thomas Addison Richards's sketch of Tallulah Falls in northeast Georgia appeared in Georgia Illustrated (1842). The sketch is one of many natural wonders drawn by Richards. \nAntique steel plate engraving on paper  9.1/2 x 7 inches\nEngraver: Rawdon Wright Hatch &amp; Smillie\nDrawn by: J.Smillie from a sketch by T.Addison Richards\nPublished by: W.H.Appleton, Grand Street\nNew York  circa 1854 for the American Landscape Annual,\nby Thomas Addison Richards 1820-1900\n\nArtist and writer Thomas Addison Richards made his engravings of the falls and the gorge a focal point of his book Georgia Illustrated, published in 1842, and made them the title piece of a collection of stories and sketches a decade later, Tallulah and Jocassee",
          "alt": "Tallulah Falls. Thomas Addison Richards's sketch of Tallulah Falls in northeast Georgia appeared in Georgia Illustrated (1842). The sketch is one of many natural wonders drawn by Richards. \nAntique steel plate engraving on paper  9.1/2 x 7 inches\nEngraver: Rawdon Wright Hatch &amp; Smillie\nDrawn by: J.Smillie from a sketch by T.Addison Richards\nPublished by: W.H.Appleton, Grand Street\nNew York  circa 1854 for the American Landscape Annual,\nby Thomas Addison Richards 1820-1900\n\nArtist and writer Thomas Addison Richards made his engravings of the falls and the gorge a focal point of his book Georgia Illustrated, published in 1842, and made them the title piece of a collection of stories and sketches a decade later, Tallulah and Jocassee",
